    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe specification required membership level 4 to be gated behind tenure of more than 365 days, so a newly created owner (zero tenure) can never exceed level 3.\n\nChanges in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`:\n\n1. **`getMembershipLevel()`** \u2014 previously started at 1, added +1 for an email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`, then hard-capped the result at 3 (with a comment that level 4 was merely \"reserved\" but never actually granted). It now adds a real fourth factor: **+1 when tenure exceeds 365 days**, and returns the level without an artificial cap. Since a new owner has zero tenure, the email + namesake factors max out at level 3.\n\n2. **New `getTenureDays()`** \u2014 computes whole days between `registrationDate` and today via `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...)`, returning `0` when `registrationDate` is unset (a brand-new owner) and never returning a negative value.\n\n3. Added the `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit` import.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` test (new owner with an email and no namesake) correctly lands at level 3, and the full suite passes.",
